# The settings window (M8) — its own folder, because it is its own window.
#
# ⚠️ Registered here for the same reason as everywhere else: quickshell loads
# through a virtual filesystem, where QML's implicit "types in my own folder"
# rule does not apply. Without an entry the type does not exist, and QML says so
# by drawing nothing. See ../common/qmldir.
#
# SettingRow and SettingGroup live here rather than in common/ because nothing
# outside this window has settings rows in it. Toggle and TextField DO live in
# common/, because they are controls rather than rows and the shell already had
# five hand-drawn text fields for want of one.
SettingsWindow 1.0 SettingsWindow.qml
SettingsContent 1.0 SettingsContent.qml
SettingsRail 1.0 SettingsRail.qml
SettingGroup 1.0 SettingGroup.qml
SettingRow 1.0 SettingRow.qml
# A row that does something instead of holding a value. Deliberately not a
# SettingRow `kind` — see the note at the top of the file.
ActionRow 1.0 ActionRow.qml
DevicePicker 1.0 DevicePicker.qml
# One program per line with its four states side by side — the App Theming page
# is a table because thirteen identical rows are not a list. Keeps SettingRow's
# one rule: it reads and writes exactly one dotted key.
ThemingRow 1.0 ThemingRow.qml
# One rounded track, N segments, exactly one true. Pulled out of ThemingRow so
# the App Theming table and a two-to-four-way choice row are the same object
# rather than two that drift. It writes nothing — the caller answers `chosen`.
Segmented 1.0 Segmented.qml
# The settings-window slider: thin track, a handle you can see, and the number
# in a box you can type in. NOT common/LevelRow, which is the volume and
# brightness bar and is right as it is where it lives.
SettingSlider 1.0 SettingSlider.qml
# Press a key, get the name niri calls it. Refuses what it cannot name.
KeyCapture 1.0 KeyCapture.qml
# The two settings that cannot be a row, each for a structural reason and each
# named in the exemption list of tests/setting-rows.sh: `outputs` is one object
# per monitor, `binds` is the whole keybinding list.
#
# ⚠️ OutputScales IS GONE — its screen-scale block is now one row among four on
# the Displays page, because a scale next to a resolution is where anybody looks
# for it, and it was the only control on Size & Shape that was not a SettingRow.
# The `outputs` exemption stands; what changed is where it is spent.
BindsList 1.0 BindsList.qml
# One monitor's row. Not a SettingRow because `outputs` has no dotted path —
# see the note at the top of the file — but composed from the same Toggle,
# Dropdown and SettingSlider so the two cannot drift apart visually.
OutputRow 1.0 OutputRow.qml
# The drag-to-arrange canvas. Its own file because it is the one control in this
# window that is a picture rather than a list.
OutputArrangement 1.0 OutputArrangement.qml
# "Reset everything" asking first, on a surface of its own. NOT a PopupWindow —
# a grab lets the compositor write `visible` and a written value replaces the
# binding, which is B25 and is why that list once never reopened.
ResetSheet 1.0 ResetSheet.qml
